type:
∀ (P : List ℕ) (a : ℕ) (b : List ℕ),
  List.foldl NimAudit.Recurrent.storeStep { acc := a, board := b } P =
    { acc := a ^^^ NimAudit.nimSum P, board := b ++ P }

∀ (N : ℕ) (c n : ℕ → Bool),
  NimAudit.CorrBridge.firstTrue
      (List.map (fun i => c i || !(List.range N).any c && n i) (List.range N)) =
    if (List.range N).any c = true then NimAudit.CorrBridge.firstTrue (List.map c (List.range N))
    else NimAudit.CorrBridge.firstTrue (List.map n (List.range N))

∀ (p : Bool) (cs : List NimAudit.AC0.Circ),
  NimAudit.ClassicalBoundary.nnf p (NimAudit.AC0.Circ.and cs) =
    if p = true then NimAudit.AC0.Circ.or (List.map (NimAudit.ClassicalBoundary.nnf p) cs)
    else NimAudit.AC0.Circ.and (List.map (NimAudit.ClassicalBoundary.nnf p) cs)

doc:
EVALUATION ACCOUNTING for one multi-head decision: rollout j makes L_j + 1 policy
evaluations; together Σ_j (L_j + 1) = (total simulated moves) + B ≤ B·(N(2^B−1)+1);
in addition there are B reset steps (one per rollout) and ONE readout evaluation.

type:
∀ (P : List ℕ),
  List.foldl NimAudit.Recurrent.storeStep { acc := 0, board := [] } P =
    { acc := NimAudit.nimSum P, board := P }

∀ (p : Bool) (cs : List NimAudit.AC0.Circ),
  NimAudit.ClassicalBoundary.nnf p (NimAudit.AC0.Circ.or cs) =
    if p = true then NimAudit.AC0.Circ.and (List.map (NimAudit.ClassicalBoundary.nnf p) cs)
    else NimAudit.AC0.Circ.or (List.map (NimAudit.ClassicalBoundary.nnf p) cs)

doc:
A readout: from board P and observed bit b, a proposed move (heap index i, new
value v), or `none` (invalid output).  No circuit restriction is imposed here;
the only property ever used is the correlation premise `CorrHyp`.

Move selector from a claimed nim-sum s: if s ≠ 0 cancel s at the first qualifying
heap; otherwise (or if no heap qualifies) subtract 1 from the first nonzero heap;
halt (`none`) only on a terminal board.

WEAK MASTERY of policy σ for the family F of initial boards and the designated role r:
from every initial board of the family from which the role has SOME winning strategy,
σ itself wins against every legal opponent strategy.

type:
∀ (s : NimAudit.Recurrent.State),
  (NimAudit.Recurrent.step s NimAudit.Recurrent.Token.sep).1 =
    { acc := 0, prev := s.acc, valid := true }

doc:
SINGLE-POLICY INFORMATION BOUND (paper Prop. single-policy-bound): if P' differs
from P in one heap h -> h', then RO_{pi_j}(P') = RO_{pi_j}(P) XOR <w_j, h XOR h'>,
a correction bit computable from the known heap values.

BYPASS BARRIERS.  Under ParityNotAC0:
(a) the complete finite-register multi-head map mhExec and the complete recurrent map
    recMove are not computed by any AC0 formula family on the encoding family;
(b) nor by any fixed-scale network family (fixed W, constant layers, polynomial size);
(c) the promised two-frame map does compute parity on promised pairs, but no AC0
    family produces the promised predecessor from the single frame.

type:
∀ (pr : ℕ → Bool) (f : ℕ → ℕ) (x : ℕ) (rest : List ℕ),
  NimAudit.SelectCircuit.firstIdx pr f (x :: rest) =
    if pr x = true then some (0, f x)
    else Option.map (fun m => (m.1 + 1, m.2)) (NimAudit.SelectCircuit.firstIdx pr f rest)

∀ (B N : ℕ) (S : NimAudit.BinReadout.BCirc) (v : ℕ → Bool) (ext : List ℕ),
  NimAudit.RolloutExec.bitStep B N S v true ext =
    NimAudit.RolloutExec.rsBits B N { board := ext, par := false, halted := false }

doc:
Output wire j: 0 summary flag; 1..B summary bits; B+1..2B difference bits;
2B+1 difference-valid; 2B+2 move flag; 2B+3 move-valid; 2B+4.. index bits (r);
2B+4+r.. move value bits (B).
